{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021309-setting-hacks-for-multi-cultural-packs","id":1021309,"title":"Setting Hacks for Multi \"Cultural\" Packs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-23T09:53:36-08:00","id":1021309,"title":"Setting Hacks for Multi \"Cultural\" Packs","content":"Unlike the clans in Vampire the Masquerade, it seems like most of the tribes in Werewolf the Apocalypse have a baked in cultural/ethnicity thing going on - they come from a certain physical location and, as of a certain time, they would have been 99.9% of the werewolves in that location. For example, if you're setting your chronicle in Dark Ages Europe, there aren't going to be Wendigo in Germany. However, it seems more fun (to me) to have packs and NPC's that come from a bunch of tribes. Is there any way to engineer things (hacking the setting somehow) so that this is possible in non-modern settings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T10:03:30-08:00","id":1021310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021309-setting-hacks-for-multi-cultural-packs#post1021309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlike the clans in Vampire the Masquerade, it seems like most of the tribes in Werewolf the Apocalypse have a baked in cultural/ethnicity thing going on - they come from a certain physical location and, as of a certain time, they would have been 99.9% of the werewolves in that location. For example, if you're setting your chronicle in Dark Ages Europe, there aren't going to be Wendigo in Germany. However, it seems more fun (to me) to have packs and NPC's that come from a bunch of tribes. Is there any way to engineer things (hacking the setting somehow) so that this is possible in non-modern settings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Even in non modern day settings, you generally have more than 1 tribe to choose from. Even a game set in the heart of the black forest in the 900s can logically have Get (obviously) plus some Talons, Gnawers, Warders of Man, CoG, Fangs, Shadowlords are close. Striders have always wandered (well for at least several thousand years). I guess my point is that outside of very specific circumstances, there is no reason a game will be limited to a single Tribe.<br /> <br /> Most Tribe's home location is set so far back, that by the last 2000 years or so they've had at least a bit of integration. Plus, Garou have incentive to actually interact with each other, and through Moon Bridges have a supernatural way to cross distances that weren't easily possible by humans during past time periods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T10:19:15-08:00","id":1021318,"title":"","content":"idpersona said most of it. Moon Bridges do for communication and travel at long distances, otherwise the Garou have a lot of interaction.<br /> <br /> What's of note, though: most places have a certain predominance. Far less than 99%, still more than today.<br /> <br /> Tribes fight a lot today. They fought a lot more before.<br /> <br /> Veil is no big deal, and Lupus Garou are a lot more common. Garou definitely live apart and independently from human society.<br /> <br /> You won't have the Pure Tribes, unless you effectively hack the setting. So, no Wendigo or Uktena. If you do hack enough for them, though, you'll also get Croatan.<br /> <br /> No Black Spiral Dancers, depending on the year. If back enough, I don't remember the year, now, you'll have the White Howlers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T10:27:21-08:00","id":1021323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021309-setting-hacks-for-multi-cultural-packs?p=1021318#post1021318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You won't have the Pure Tribes, unless you effectively hack the setting. So, no Wendigo or Uktena. If you do hack enough for them, though, you'll also get Croatan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Had forgotten to address the Pure Lands Tribes. I suppose you would have to &quot;hack&quot; the setting to get them in, but it is doable. They are just going to be special snowflakes, depending on where/when the game is set.<br /> <br /> I know the Wyld West books had a write up for the Bunyip because they were a possibility. I've seen (in small numbers) Uktena in a period Hengeyokai game. There were leftovers from crossing the land bridge if I remember correctly.<br /> <br /> Most of these sorts of issues are covered in the period setting books, with the DA books being having the most info. I have Shattered Dreams but haven't read through it yet so I don't know what, if anything, it has to say of the subject. Tribal tensions are much higher in times past, but for a game with PCs it's generally nothing that's insurmountable.<br /> <br /> btw, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>, from the lengths of your most recent posts, I'm guessing your tendinitis is getting at least somewhat better. good to see it (if I'm right).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T10:45:02-08:00","id":1021331,"title":"","content":"Cool thanks for all the clarifications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T12:43:06-08:00","id":1021367,"title":"","content":"Be welcome, its an interesting period for the setting, but receives far less attention for werewolves than for Vampires and Mages, at least from players.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar805_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"805\" data-vbnamecard=\"805\">idpersona</a>, I'm getting better, yes, thank you. I'll probably be able to go back to work on next Tuesday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T13:00:33-08:00","id":1021375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021309-setting-hacks-for-multi-cultural-packs#post1021309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlike the clans in Vampire the Masquerade, it seems like most of the tribes in Werewolf the Apocalypse have a baked in cultural/ethnicity thing going on - they come from a certain physical location and, as of a certain time, they would have been 99.9% of the werewolves in that location. For example, if you're setting your chronicle in Dark Ages Europe, there aren't going to be Wendigo in Germany. However, it seems more fun (to me) to have packs and NPC's that come from a bunch of tribes. Is there any way to engineer things (hacking the setting somehow) so that this is possible in non-modern settings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right now in London they're digging up a graveyard full of Roman-era skeletons whose skeletons are clearly Sub-Saharan African, i.e. Black people have been in Britain since before there was an England. So while there was not much population mixing and permanent relocation going on, individual people have been migrating or wandering for thousands of years. There's even some evidence that continents-spanning trade predates agriculture.<br /> <br /> So while 80% of your Sept is probably all one Tribe, there's plenty of possibility for one or two individuals to be from somewhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T13:55:14-08:00","id":1021395,"title":"","content":"I think the only limitations you really have is that the Pure One tribes and everyone else is kept separate. But even here if you really want some unique tribe, someone got lost on a moon bridge or the umbra and ended up here.<br /> <br /> No matter where you set the chronicle, you can almost always include the Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, and Silver Fangs anywhere. And as long as its a time period where there are lots of wolves, the Red Talons as well.<br /> <br /> The other tribes can almost always be justified from ethnic migrations at some point in time or visiting Anruth. Historically there have been lots of places where there have been Celts, Germans, Greeks, etc. all over the place. And that is not to mention some leftover group from during the Stone Age where our historical knowledge is non-existent.<br /> <br /> I found it strange that in the Dark Ages book the Stargazers are not listed. The tribe might be particularly strong in the Himalayas and Tibet, but I always associated the tribe with mountain tops and not with the East. Certainly in the earliest sourcebooks, the rare Stargazers had plenty of western members. There is no reason why there wouldn't be some Stargazer caern in the Alps in Europe. Unfortunately, I think this was a case where early attempt at diversity meant people tried to make it the &quot;eastern tribe&quot;.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, you can always tie additional ethnicities into a tribe. The ethnic focus from kinfolk is an artifact or effect of the tribe's history, not a cause. I never understood why the Hakken went from Shadow Lords in Japan to &quot;Well, they aren't Shadow Lords, just children of Grandfather Thunder who are a different tribe&quot;. But that is the definition of a tribe - people who are the totem's children! If you want Hungarian or Finnish Fianna, go for it! If you think the Celtic invasion of Galatia in Anatolia included Garou kinfolk, then add your Greek or Turkish Fianna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T20:39:42-08:00","id":1021465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1021309-setting-hacks-for-multi-cultural-packs?p=1021318#post1021318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No Black Spiral Dancers, depending on the year. If back enough, I don't remember the year, now, you'll have the White Howlers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Howlers fell around AD 200, so they will not only be around for a Dark Ages campaign, they'll have been established for about a thousand years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T00:48:44-08:00","id":1021491,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a>, that's far earlier than I thought, thank you.<br /> <br /> Now, I remember something about the Stargazers being a relatively new tribe. Someone knows more about their history?<br /> <br /> Pure Tribes can be easily hacked on the game through the reasons given above, either Umbral happenstance or remnants from their old journey. The Siberakh stand as evidence of the possibility.<br /> <br /> Either way, Umbral happenstance probably occurred with some regularity. An individual Garou, or even a little pack, of a &quot;lost&quot; tribe showing up from an Umbral quest shouldn't be that much of a strange thing for the Garou. It happens, and do not create any through path back, so they are probably stuck were they came to, no reliably way created to communication or travel between their communities. So it can be used both for Pure Tribes being present in Europe, or for European Garou being present at the Pure Lands way before true contact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T17:28:56-08:00","id":1025205,"title":"","content":"Never forget that spirits can play a role in a pack or individual Garou being &quot;out of place&quot;. A spirit playing a role could even be the focal point of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}